course: dictionary
lesson: 9224
title: Someone: a person we do not name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Someone» is a pronoun. It stands in for a person when we do not say who that person is. «Someone ate my chips» means a person ate them, and the speaker does not name them.
explain: The clues are in the words around it. Look at the verb that comes after «someone»: ate, asked, designed. «If someone asks you to keep a secret» tells you a person is doing the asking, even though nobody is named.
explain: Sometimes «someone» hints at a person we know, or teases a person who is right there. «Someone's grumpy» said with a sly look is a joke about the person in front of you. Check the tone and the situation before you decide what it means.
explain: Stiff, formal writing uses other words for a person, such as «an individual». Try the swap test: put «a person» into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have understood it.
fact: Someone is a pronoun, a word that stands in for a noun.
fact: «Someone» means a person, but we do not say who.
fact: «Someone» can also mean an important person, as in «she wants to be someone».
fact: «Someone else» and «someone or other» are common phrases.
fact: In casual talk, «someone» can be a pointed hint or a tease; in formal writing, people say «an individual» instead.
exercise: «Almost everything you touch was designed by someone: the tick on your trainers, the font in your book.» Who designed these things? | The weather | A teacher in the school | The trainers themselves | *A person nobody names
exercise: «If someone you don't know asks you to go with them, say no and tell an adult.» What should you do? | Go with them if they seem nice | Tell them your address | *Say no and tell an adult | Keep it secret from your parents
exercise: Which word is a stiffer, formal word for someone? | yesterday | *an individual | forever | a biscuit
test: «Someone's grumpy», said with a sly look, is mainly what? | A map of the town | *A tease about a person who is right there | A weather report | A question about the time
test: In «she wants to be someone», what does someone mean? | A small animal | Nobody at all | *An important person | A stranger in the street
exam: In «If someone tells you a hurtful thing another person said, check with that person directly», what does someone refer to? | A word for silence | *A person we do not name | The teacher | A type of hurtful thing
